WEBVTT

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:08.385
Hey, I'm Josh Radner, and I am joined as ever by my dear friend, Craig Thomas.
嘿，我是乔什·拉德纳，一如既往，我的好朋友克雷格·托马斯也加入了我的节目。

00:00:08.385 --> 00:00:09.654
Hello, Josh.
你好，乔什。

00:00:09.654 --> 00:00:11.028
Hello, Craig.
你好，克雷格。

00:00:11.028 --> 00:00:13.988
It's great to see you again.
很高兴再次见到你。

00:00:13.988 --> 00:00:25.088
This is a bonus episode of how we made your mother, and it's something we like to call general questions.
这是《老爸老妈的浪漫史》制作花絮的特别番外篇，我们喜欢把它叫做“常规问题”。

00:00:25.088 --> 00:00:26.991
General questions.
常规问题。

00:00:26.991 --> 00:00:32.700
So we're joined also by our pal and producer Alec Lev.
所以我们的朋友兼制片人亚历克·莱夫也加入了我们。

00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:33.862
Hello Alec.
你好，亚历克。

00:00:33.862 --> 00:00:35.131
Hello, Josh.
你好，乔什。

00:00:35.131 --> 00:00:35.765
Hello.
你好。

00:00:35.765 --> 00:00:40.100
Do you have any general questions for us?
你有什么常规问题要问我们吗？

00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:41.179
I am honest, my man.
说实话，兄弟。

00:00:41.179 --> 00:00:42.020
Let's do it.
来吧。

00:00:42.020 --> 00:00:43.020
All right.
好的。

00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:44.340
You missed your salute, Craig.
克雷格，你漏掉你的军礼了。

00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:45.340
I'm sorry.
我很抱歉。

00:00:45.340 --> 00:00:46.340
Excellent.
太棒了。

00:00:46.340 --> 00:00:48.340
Oh, awful.
哦，糟透了。

00:00:48.340 --> 00:00:49.340
Yeah.
是啊。

00:00:49.340 --> 00:00:50.340
So I was never in the army.
所以我从来没当过兵。

00:00:50.340 --> 00:00:52.899
I never will be in the army.
我以后也绝不会当兵。

00:00:52.899 --> 00:00:53.420
Yeah.
是啊。

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:55.219
Hi, guys.
大家好。

00:00:55.219 --> 00:01:03.939
This week, people are curious, I would say, in the large about how TV kind of gets made.
本周，人们普遍对电视剧是怎么拍出来的很感兴趣，我想可以说是这样。

00:01:03.939 --> 00:01:04.739
There's a lot of questions.
有很多问题。

00:01:04.739 --> 00:01:08.219
And by the way, this is about episode three sweet taste of liberty.
顺便说一下，这是关于第三集《自由的甜味》。

00:01:08.219 --> 00:01:11.120
These are questions about episode three, right?
这些都是关于第三集的问题，对吧？

00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:12.200
It is, that is correct.
是的，没错。

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:19.079
There were a lot of questions about Liberty Bells and licking things, and we're gonna focus more on the production side of things.
有很多关于自由钟和舔东西的问题，但我们将更多地关注制作方面的事情。

00:01:19.079 --> 00:01:22.719
I'm just gonna give you a couple examples, but then I'm gonna kind of broaden out the question.
我只举几个例子，然后我会把问题稍微扩展一下。

00:01:22.719 --> 00:01:32.599
So, LJ spectrum asks, how far into filming did you create the opening sequence and bar photos?
所以，LJ spectrum问：拍到第几集时，你们才制作了开场镜头和酒吧照片？

00:01:32.599 --> 00:01:36.200
Was it specifically for this episode and then turned into the opening montage?
这专门是为这一集拍的，然后才变成了开场剪辑吗？

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:37.159
How did you do that?
你们是怎么做到的？

00:01:37.159 --> 00:01:46.549
And then Oscar underscore Cal Vajor says just out of curiosity is this the same basement we see later on at Stella's house.
然后Oscar underscore Cal Vajor说，出于好奇，这和后来在斯特拉家里看到的地下室是同一个吗？

00:01:47.790 --> 00:01:53.689
So just thinking about how, yeah, I don't know, but the answer to that or what?
所以就在想，是的，我不知道，但是有这个的答案吗？

00:01:53.689 --> 00:01:55.290
I've never actually seen this show.
我其实从没看过这部剧。

00:01:55.290 --> 00:01:59.290
I don't have any, I have no answers to any of this.
我对这些完全没有任何答案。

00:01:59.290 --> 00:02:03.370
I heard it so, obviously we have viewers who know a lot more than we do.
我听说过，所以很显然，我们的观众比我们知道得要多得多。

00:02:04.769 --> 00:02:09.490
But I think what this is going to is just kind How do you make a television show?
但我认为这正说明了一个问题：电视剧到底是怎么拍出来的？

00:02:09.490 --> 00:02:14.210
And I think if we can walk through one thing, we'll answer a lot of people's questions.
我想如果我们能经历一件事，就能回答很多人的问题。

00:02:14.210 --> 00:02:20.849
And maybe we could do a helium style of, how did Craig see a week of production and how did Josh see a week of production?
也许我们可以用一种交替的方式：克雷格眼中一周的制作是怎样的，而乔什眼中一周的制作又是怎样的？

00:02:20.849 --> 00:02:22.449
How was this show made?
这部剧是怎么制作出来的？

00:02:22.449 --> 00:02:23.569
Can I go back to a thing?
我能回到刚才的一个问题吗？

00:02:23.569 --> 00:02:27.090
Because I actually, I really like the first question about the open credit sequence.
因为我其实，我真的很喜欢关于开场演职员表序列的第一个问题。

00:02:27.090 --> 00:02:27.650
Me too.
我也是。

00:02:27.650 --> 00:02:28.449
Great, great.
太好了，太好了。

00:02:28.449 --> 00:02:38.449
So, and we can get back to this out because I like this too, but Craig, where did the idea for the opening credits This is kind of like friends, pictures, kind of popular.
所以，我们等下可以再回到这个话题，因为我也喜欢这个，但是克雷格，开场字幕的想法是从哪来的？这有点像《老友记》那种照片形式，当时挺受欢迎的。

00:02:38.449 --> 00:02:39.449
That was from the beginning.
那是从一开始就有了。

00:02:39.449 --> 00:02:43.090
That was when we were writing the pilot, when the pilot got picked up.
那是我们在写试播集时，试播集被预订的时候。

00:02:43.090 --> 00:02:44.689
We always had that idea.
我们一直都有那个想法。

00:02:44.689 --> 00:02:47.169
This is a weird thing that I don't think I've ever talked about.
这是一件很奇怪的事，我觉得我以前从来没说过。

00:02:47.169 --> 00:02:53.009
For a minute, I remember Carter Bay's, I think it might have been his concept to begin with.
有一会儿，我记得卡特·贝斯，我觉得这可能一开始就是他的概念。

00:02:53.009 --> 00:02:58.810
And the way he wanted to do it at first was pictures of just young people in New York, not even our cast.
他一开始想用的方式是，只放纽约年轻人的照片，甚至都不是我们的演员。

00:02:58.810 --> 00:03:02.770
This very abstracted idea of like, you're just seeing youth in New York.
这种非常抽象的想法，就像是：你只是在看纽约的青春。

00:03:02.770 --> 00:03:03.770
It could be anyone.
可以是任何人。

00:03:03.770 --> 00:03:06.849
seeing this pastiche of New York City and people out.
看到这种纽约市和人们外出的拼贴画。

00:03:06.849 --> 00:03:08.569
And it's just them and their friends, blah, blah, blah.
而且只有他们和他们的朋友，巴拉巴拉。

00:03:08.569 --> 00:03:09.810
And I think we gained it out.
我想我们把这个给推演出来了。

00:03:09.810 --> 00:03:11.650
We started looking at it, we're like, this is too weird.
我们开始看着它，然后我们想：这太奇怪了。

00:03:11.650 --> 00:03:12.490
Who are these people?
这些人是谁？

00:03:12.490 --> 00:03:13.330
These aren't the same.
这些演员不对。

00:03:13.330 --> 00:03:15.289
I mean, this is in the cast of the show.
我的意思是，这不是剧中的演员。

00:03:15.289 --> 00:03:16.250
And that was how we learned.
这就是我们吸取教训的方式。

00:03:16.250 --> 00:03:18.729
I mean, it was sort of a little too artsy of an idea, maybe.
我的意思是，这可能算是一个有点太文艺的想法了。

00:03:18.729 --> 00:03:21.090
And then we realized, let's get the cast to do this.
然后我们意识到，让演员来做这个吧。

00:03:21.090 --> 00:03:24.689
But if I remember, currently, Josh, I think we did the pilot, right?
但如果我没记错的话，乔什，我觉得我们拍了试播集，对吧？

00:03:24.689 --> 00:03:25.969
We did a little photo shoot.
我们拍了一组小照片。

00:03:25.969 --> 00:03:27.770
We did a photo shoot right away.
我们马上就拍了一组照片。

00:03:27.770 --> 00:03:30.409
Like in the booth, kind of like Candid's.
就像在照相亭里那样，有点像抓拍。

00:03:30.409 --> 00:03:32.370
I remember, did Jason hold the camera?
我记得，是杰森拿着相机吗？

00:03:32.370 --> 00:03:34.090
Was it like a selfie?
就像是自拍吗？

00:03:34.090 --> 00:03:43.729
I think sometimes you guys were selfieing and I think sometimes literally Pam Fryman, our director, I think was like shooting it on at what at that time was like a crappy like disposable camera.
我觉得有时候是你们在自拍，而且我觉得有时候确实是我们的导演帕姆·弗莱曼，当时正用一台现在看来很烂的一次性相机在拍。

00:03:43.729 --> 00:03:45.009
These were on phone packs, right?
这些都是用这种傻瓜相机拍的，对吧？

00:03:45.009 --> 00:03:52.129
And you see that Lily, it looks, and it dates the show so much, but you see in titles that Lily is holding that old disposable camera.
你看莉莉手里拿的，它让这部剧充满了时代的印记，但你在片头里能看到莉莉拿着那个老式的一次性相机。

00:03:52.129 --> 00:03:54.009
That's literally what they're still getting.
这确实就是他们当时用的那种。

00:03:54.009 --> 00:03:57.289
So they're placed on tables at weddings, you know, there's still in use.
所以它们被放在婚礼的桌子上，你知道的，现在还在使用。

00:03:57.289 --> 00:03:58.370
Ironically.
具有讽刺意味的是。

00:03:58.370 --> 00:04:05.969
Where the like color scheme come up with like that kind of seepia, so I really like the kind of rods and yellows and.
那种复古的色调是怎么来的，比如那种棕褐色、红色和黄色的感觉？

00:04:05.969 --> 00:04:14.169
We said we wanted to feel like memories, like these sort of old tinge sort of like seepia tone, sort of like just this feeling of these exist as memories in someone's mind.
我们说过，我们希望它感觉像回忆，就像这种带点老旧色彩、有点棕褐色的基调，就像是在某人脑海中作为回忆存在的那种感觉。

00:04:14.169 --> 00:04:15.490
Yeah.
是啊。

00:04:15.490 --> 00:04:16.329
Yeah.
是啊。

00:04:16.329 --> 00:04:20.089
And when did you guys hit on using the solid song or the end of Hey Beautiful?
你们是什么时候决定用The Sol Seeds的歌或者《Hey Beautiful》的结尾的？

00:04:22.019 --> 00:04:28.540
I think we, for a minute, we wanted to use, I've never said this either, I think, we wanted to use a replacement song.
我想有一会儿，我们想用，我也从来没说过这个，我想，我们想用替换乐队（The Replacements）的歌。

00:04:28.540 --> 00:04:33.696
The band replacement, Carter and I are huge fans replacements card turned me into a replacement span.
The Replacements乐队，卡特和我都是The Replacements的超级粉丝，卡特让我迷上了The Replacements。

00:04:33.696 --> 00:04:39.261
And we were talking about using, um, I think we're going to, I think we're going to use the song unsatisfied.
我们在讨论用，嗯，我想我们要用，我想我们要用《Unsatisfied》这首歌。

00:04:39.261 --> 00:04:46.511
Like, and literally, I think we cut a version of the main titles that was pictures of total strangers set to the replacement song unsatisfied.
真的，我想我们剪辑了一个版本的片头，里面全是不认识的陌生人的照片，配上The Replacements的歌《Unsatisfied》。

00:04:46.511 --> 00:04:51.003
It looks like it's just opening titles to an entirely different show called unsatisfied.
看起来就像是一部完全不同的电视剧的片头，剧名就叫《不满意》（Unsatisfied）。

00:04:51.003 --> 00:04:56.619
It was utterly confusing and it was a complete fail, but it's what taught us that we needed it to be our cast.
这让人感到无比困惑，彻底搞砸了，但正是这件事教会了我们：我们需要用我们自己的演员。

00:04:56.619 --> 00:05:04.379
And the idea of photos and memories like that, that was always the idea, but we had to do a bad like misguided version of that to get to what it became.
照片和类似回忆的想法，这个想法一直都在，但我们必须先做一个糟糕的、被误导的版本，才能最终变成后来的样子。

00:05:04.379 --> 00:05:08.540
And isn't Barney's last name after a guitar like a replacement?
巴尼的姓氏是不是取自某个吉他手，就像The Replacements乐队里的那样？

00:05:08.540 --> 00:05:09.686
Yeah, Barney Stinson.
是的，巴尼·斯廷森（Barney Stinson）。

00:05:09.686 --> 00:05:15.579
Stinson, Tommy Stinson is the bass player for the replacements, and that is a shout out to the replacements.
斯廷森，汤米·斯廷森（Tommy Stinson）是The Replacements的贝斯手，这是对The Replacements的致敬。

00:05:15.579 --> 00:05:22.459
Who again, and we really wanted to unsatisfied to be the song, and then we got the bill for what that would cost every week.
再说一次，我们真的很想把《Unsatisfied》作为主题曲，然后我们收到了每周需要支付多少版权费的账单。

00:05:23.339 --> 00:05:27.978
And then we said, what if we put our own band song on there, And we get that money.
然后我们说，如果我们把我们自己乐队的歌放上去，然后我们拿到那笔钱呢？

00:05:27.978 --> 00:05:30.773
And they said, what about one tenth of that money?
他们说，那十分之一的钱怎么样？

00:05:30.773 --> 00:05:31.500
I said souls.
我说：The Solids（乐队名）。

00:05:33.819 --> 00:05:36.601
Craig, did you need to get approval at this point?
克雷格，你当时需要获得批准吗？

00:05:36.601 --> 00:05:40.383
Did the studio or network have to like, look at that title sequence?
制片厂或电视台必须过目并审核那个片头序列吗？

00:05:40.383 --> 00:05:40.884
Oh, yeah.
哦，是的。

00:05:40.884 --> 00:05:41.385
Oh, yeah.
哦，是的。

00:05:41.385 --> 00:05:45.334
That thing is like tested and game down and sent up and down the chain.
那个东西经过了测试、推敲，并在整个层级中上下传达。

00:05:45.334 --> 00:05:48.060
It's, it's, it's the branding of the show, right?
这就是，这就是，这就是节目的品牌形象，对吧？

00:05:48.060 --> 00:05:50.069
It's like the brand does become so iconic.
就像这个品牌真的变得如此具有标志性。

00:05:50.069 --> 00:05:52.987
And what's amazing about it now is like, I see people online.
现在最让人惊叹的是，我看到网上的那些人。

00:05:52.987 --> 00:06:02.220
I see people on socials like them and their friends are literally shot for shot recreating how I met your mother photos from the opening main titles and they're doing it with their own friends.
我在社交媒体上看到，他们和朋友们一帧一帧地完美还原《老爸老妈浪漫史》片头主标题里的照片，他们是用自己的朋友来拍的。

00:06:02.220 --> 00:06:08.800
And I find that so moving and pointing like we've passed this baton onto this younger generation who are now like enacting it.
我觉得这太感人、太深刻了，就像我们把这根接力棒交给了现在正在模仿它的年轻一代。

00:06:08.800 --> 00:06:23.579
And it's their way of saying we're making our own memories now I think which is a story that Josh you've told to about a fan told you said do you I realize I'm living these memories now and that's I love the idea that like young people watching the show are creating that themselves.
这也是他们表达“我们现在正在创造属于自己的回忆”的一种方式吧，乔希，你之前也讲过一个故事，有个粉丝告诉你，她说：“你知道吗？我意识到我现在正在经历这些回忆。”我特别喜欢这种想法，看节目的年轻人正在亲手创造这些。

00:06:23.579 --> 00:06:24.079
Yeah.
是的。

00:06:24.079 --> 00:06:25.747
So speaking of memories.
所以说到回忆。

00:06:25.747 --> 00:06:43.812
So Josh, so at this point when week three of producing this show, obviously spread over time between the pilot and the second episode, but what was your week like, at least in this first season, how did that script first come to on what day rehearsal blocking?
那么乔希，在制作这部节目的第三周这个时候，虽然试播集和第二集之间显然隔了一段时间，但你的那一周是怎么过的？至少在第一季的时候，那个剧本是哪天出来的？什么时候排练、走位？

00:06:43.660 --> 00:06:45.502
How did it look for you?
对你来说是什么样的？

00:06:45.502 --> 00:06:51.259
My memory is in Craig maybe like we would get an envelope over the weekend.
我的记忆是，也许我和克雷格会在周末收到一个信封。

00:06:51.259 --> 00:07:02.006
Yeah, like on a Sunday, I think maybe sometimes Friday, sometimes Friday, but hard copies in a in a Manila envelope kind of like waiting at your door.
对，就像在周日，我想有时也可能是周五，但都是纸质版，装在马尼拉纸信封里，放在你家门口那种。

00:07:02.006 --> 00:07:05.660
Yeah, and you'd read and that was the table script.
对，然后你就会读，那就是围读剧本。

00:07:05.660 --> 00:07:09.759
That was the script we were going to read Monday at like 10 a.m.
那是我们周一上午10点左右要读的剧本。

00:07:09.759 --> 00:07:10.272
Correct.
没错。

00:07:10.272 --> 00:07:12.706
So the actors would come in at 10 a.m.
所以演员们会在周一上午10点

00:07:12.706 --> 00:07:13.347
on Monday.
来到现场。

00:07:13.347 --> 00:07:14.884
We'd sit around a table.
我们围坐在一张桌子旁。

00:07:14.884 --> 00:07:16.998
There was a great spread of food.
那里有非常丰盛的食物。

00:07:16.998 --> 00:07:22.379
All the writers were where their producers, the department heads would come to that.
所有的编剧、制片人、各部门负责人都会来参加。

00:07:22.379 --> 00:07:23.220
Yeah.
对。

00:07:23.220 --> 00:07:24.699
And we'd like to get around this.
我们会聚在一起……

00:07:24.699 --> 00:07:29.220
Yeah, we, the studio execs network execs, we'd sit around and it was, it was not a high pressure.
对，我们，还有工作室高管、电视台高管，我们围坐在一起，而且那并没有太大的压力。

00:07:29.220 --> 00:07:32.139
I never felt beyond maybe the pilot table read.
除了试播集的围读桌上可能有一点，我从来没觉得压力有多大。

00:07:32.139 --> 00:07:36.259
That was always like the chillest low pressure kind of thing.
那一直是一种最轻松、压力最小的事情。

00:07:36.259 --> 00:07:44.459
So we'd read the script, Pam would read the stage directions and you and Carter would flank Pam, I remember.
所以我们会读剧本，帕姆会读舞台说明，我记得你和卡特分别坐在帕姆的两侧。

00:07:44.459 --> 00:07:45.300
Yeah.
是的。

00:07:45.300 --> 00:07:49.899
And by the way, just to say counterpoint, I was wildly nervous for all 200 native tables.
顺便说一下，作为反衬，我其实对所有那200场母语剧本围读都感到极度紧张。

00:07:49.899 --> 00:07:50.899
You were.
你是这样的。

00:07:50.899 --> 00:07:51.899
Okay.
好吧。

00:07:51.899 --> 00:07:52.899
Well, miserably anxious.
嗯，痛苦地焦虑。

00:07:52.899 --> 00:07:53.899
I shocked that you weren't.
我很震惊你居然不紧张。

00:07:53.899 --> 00:07:55.259
But think about writer brand.
但想想编剧的品牌。

